211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (Super Science Saturday is an engaging event that our team, Team 1711, has proudly hosted for 16 years. This initiative aims to inspire children aged 4 to 14 through more than 12 distinct experiments, each designed to teach scientific principles in an enjoyable and innovative manner. Annually, we inspire over 500 children through our efforts. This year marked a significant milestone, as we hosted the event for the first time in our school's new STEM space, providing young participants with a glimpse into their future within the FIRST community. Additionally, we showcased our robot, further cultivating interest in robotics. The event's enduring success is reflected in the fact that many current team members recall their own experiences attending this event.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (A new initiative that our team has taken this year is LEGO STEM camps. This introduces kids in grades 3-5 to the fundamentals of FIRST. At these camps, we hosted over 60 kids, teaching them the basics of robotics through the same parts used in FLL. This led to more engagement with FLL in our community and even caused the formation of an independent FLL team. This impacted our community by building up the next generation of FIRST participants and creating a love for STEM in our youth community.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
