295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Our team is immensely proud of our Subject Matter Expert \(SME\) leadership system, which significantly enhances the diversity of our team's skills and fosters an inclusive environment for all interested in STEM. This framework allows multiple individuals to become SMEs within a single subteam, with their designation based purely on merit and skills demonstrated over time. Consequently, we are thrilled to report that 42% of our leadership is female, and 40% of leadership roles are held by individuals from cultural minorities or the LGBTQ+ community. Had we adopted a leadership model based on popularity or appointments by mentors, we might not have achieved these remarkable results due to the persistent cultural barriers within the STEM community.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Out team has introduced the "SME Constitution," a document that outlines the formal process for becoming a Subject Matter Expert \(SME\) for a designated subteam. This constitution provides clear guidelines and details the responsibilities associated with the role. We believe the system is well-structured and straightforward. To qualify as an SME, one must deliver a presentation to the entire team about their specific subteam, possess a Varsity Letter, and obtain approval from a mentor with at least three-quarters support.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
